## GREEN evidence (after the fix)

**Test result — `cargo test -p ium-core --test supervisor`:**

```
running 6 tests
test cancel_after_done_is_rejected_and_cancel_is_never_a_failure ... ok
test cancel_mid_running_lands_canceled_in_the_journal_and_survives_reopen ... ok
test drive_is_callable_off_the_runtime_thread ... ok
test pause_then_resume_through_the_supervisor_re_spawns_to_done ... ok
test supervisor_drive_spawns_the_transfer_and_reaches_done ... ok
test with_handle_constructs_off_runtime_and_drives_off_runtime ... ok

test result: ok. 6 passed; 0 failed
```

The RED test now passes: a supervisor constructed inside a runtime, driven from a
thread with **no tokio context** (the GTK main thread's permanent state), drives the
job to `Done`. The second new test pins the shell's exact shape — `Supervisor::with_handle`
constructed **and** driven on a context-less thread → `Done`.

**The fix:**

* `ium-core/src/supervisor.rs` — `Supervisor` captures a `tokio::runtime::Handle`
  at construction (`new()` via `Handle::try_current().ok()`, or explicitly via the
  new `Supervisor::with_handle(manager, handle)` for context-less hosts); `drive()`
  spawns through the stored handle, falling back to the ambient context only when
  nothing is stored, and panics honestly (with the repair in the message) only when
  a host constructed context-less AND gave no handle — a host bug, not an ambient
  accident.
* `ium-app/src-tauri/src/lib.rs` — setup passes tauri's async-runtime tokio handle:
  `tauri::async_runtime::block_on(async { tokio::runtime::Handle::current() })`
  (note: `tauri::async_runtime::handle()` returns tauri's own `RuntimeHandle`
  enum, not the tokio handle — the block_on form reads the real `Handle` with
  verified-stable APIs).

**Full gates on the same tree:** `cargo fmt --all -- --check` clean;
`cargo clippy -p ium-core --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean;
`cargo test -p ium-core` = **87/87 green** (adapter_s3 23, adapter_tus 12,
adaptive_resplit 1, enospc drills 3, finishing_cancel 1, frozen_link_resplit 1,
http_one_shot 5, integration 22, lone_worker_eviction 1, real_data 3, s3_drill 1,
slow_connection 1, soak_bounds 1, supervisor 6, tus_drill 1, verify_is_required 1,
verify_repair 3).

